-- Version 22 → 23: projects become an ordered list.
--
-- Until now the picker sorted projects by name — `selectAll ... ORDER BY name`
-- in Projects.sq — and a system administrator could not arrange them. But which
-- project comes first is a curation decision, the same one the vocabulary tables
-- already let a project owner make (see Labels.sq), and alphabetical is not a
-- decision, it is what you get when nobody made one. LNL-93 gives that decision a
-- home in the instance settings dialog.
--
-- ── The back-fill ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
--
-- Exactly 9.sqm's shape, which did this for labels and components. `ALTER TABLE
-- ADD COLUMN` can only supply a constant, so every row would land on 0 and the
-- order become arbitrary — worse than alphabetical, not better. The UPDATE seeds
-- each row's position with the rank it already had: its place in the instance's
-- alphabetical list. So the upgrade changes nothing anybody can see, and the
-- feature starts from the order they are used to.
--
-- The rank is a correlated count of the rows that sort before this one, with id
-- as the tie-break. `name` is COLLATE NOCASE and UNIQUE across the instance, so
-- two names cannot actually tie — but a comparison that could return 0 for two
-- different rows would give them the same position, and the arrows would then
-- swap two rows that both claim the same slot. The id costs nothing and removes
-- the question. `p2.name < projects.name` uses the column's own NOCASE collation
-- on both sides, the same comparison `ORDER BY name` was making, so the seeded
-- order is exactly the list the old `selectAll` returned.
--
-- The DEFAULT 0 matches the column as Projects.sq now declares it: a fresh
-- database must end up with the same PRAGMA as a migrated one, and MigrationTest
-- is what enforces that.

ALTER TABLE projects ADD COLUMN position INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0;

UPDATE projects SET position = (
    SELECT COUNT(*) FROM projects p2
    WHERE p2.name < projects.name OR (p2.name = projects.name AND p2.id < projects.id)
);
